# Roadbook compose configuration (phase 5 BRIEF §1.2). Copy to .env and edit;
# .env is gitignored and never committed. Every knob has a working default —
# an empty .env (or none) brings the stack up. Nothing here is a coordinate,
# a region, or anything about a specific user (CLAUDE.md invariant 9).

# Password for the compose-internal Postgres. The database is not published
# to the host; this credential never crosses the compose network boundary.
#POSTGRES_PASSWORD=roadbook

# Map style URL. The default is the Roadbook light style shipped with the
# app (derived from OpenFreeMap Liberty; its tiles, glyphs and sprites still
# come from OpenFreeMap). Tile fetches are the one browser request that
# leaves the self-hosted boundary (the viewport leaks to the style's tile
# host); point this at a style with self-hosted tiles to close even that.
#ROADBOOK_MAP_STYLE=https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty

# Name suggestion at confirm time: none (default) or nominatim. Opt-in — a
# self-hosted product makes no surprise network calls.
#ROADBOOK_GEOCODER=none
#ROADBOOK_NOMINATIM_URL=https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org

# Optional routing profile only: the OSRM dataset base name under
# data/osrm/, as printed by scripts/osrm-setup.sh (e.g. iceland-latest).
# Used by `docker compose --profile routing up`; the default stack ignores
# it entirely.
#OSRM_DATA=iceland-latest
